{"key":"airtemp","updated":"2026-10-31","label":"Air temperature","title":"Air temperature compared with normal","subtitle":"Jul–Sep 2026, against the same months in 1991–2020","source":"gridMET daily maximum and minimum temperature, averaged by parish","demo":false,"build":1,"categories":[{"key":"very_cool","label":"Much cooler","note":"coldest 10% of years","color":"#2c7bb6"},{"key":"cool","label":"Cooler","note":"coldest 10 to 30% of years","color":"#abd9e9"},{"key":"normal","label":"Near normal","note":"middle 40% of years","color":"#f3efe4"},{"key":"warm","label":"Warmer","note":"warmest 10 to 30% of years","color":"#fdae61"},{"key":"very_warm","label":"Much warmer","note":"warmest 10% of years","color":"#d7191c"},{"key":"not_rated","label":"Not rated","note":"too few years or days missing","color":"#bdbdbd"}],"rank":{"high":"Warmest compared with normal","low":"Coolest compared with normal","note":"Ranked by the difference from the 1991–2020 mean temperature (°C)."},"how":"How far the average air temperature of the last three complete months (Jul–Sep 2026) is from the average of the same months in 1991 to 2020. The mean temperature is the average of each day's high and low. The colour shows where this year ranks among those 30 years, so \"much warmer\" means among the warmest 10%.","limits":["gridMET is a 4 km grid that mixes PRISM (built from weather stations) with a land model. It is an estimate, not a thermometer reading.","A parish value is the average of the grid cells inside it.","Mean temperature hides hot afternoons and cool nights, and it does not count heat days or frost.","The newest days are provisional and get revised for a few weeks. A month only counts when every day is in the record."],"credits":[{"text":"Temperature: gridMET, Abatzoglou, J.T. (2013), Int. J. Climatology 33: 121-131","url":"https://www.climatologylab.org/gridmet.html"},{"text":"Parish boundaries: US Census Bureau cartographic boundary files (public domain)","url":"https://www.c